# RETIRED 2026-10-16. This is the PUBLIC half of the age keypair that used to
# decrypt a keypair-encrypted server/secrets.env.age. That ciphertext has been
# replaced with a passphrase-encrypted one, and the private key
# (server/age-key.txt) is gone — it cannot decrypt anything here any more.
#
# Kept because it is a PUBLIC key (safe to publish) and because the retired
# ciphertext still exists in git history, where this is the only record of which
# key opened it.
#
# The key line is FIRST because callers pass this file's text as a single `-r`
# recipient, and that form cannot tolerate comments. Verified 2026-10-16:
#   age -R <this file>          → works, comments ignored
#   age -r "$(cat this file)"   → "invalid recipient encoding: mixed case"
# Both forms work when the key is the first line, so it stays first.
